# This repo (Python)

User-level jexreffy standards still apply. Here:

- Python 3.11+ style: `X | None`, Ruff (`E`, `F`, `I`, `UP`).
- Domain code in `src/sbm/`; keep CLI and FastAPI thin.
- Automated suite (`pytest` + `ruff`) covers odds math, leakage, and mode isolation. That suite is the PR gate — not a future AI QA bot.
- Simulation vs Live ledgers never mix.
- Historical P&L uses research windows (warmup / search / holdout); 2026 is hands-off for backtests.
